# Design fills

When Figma is full, partial, or missing: Figma wins where it exists; the codebase wins for the rest. Invent layout composition, not a new visual language.

## Rules

- Prefer the nearest sibling screen and existing components/tokens over inventing new patterns
- No new colors, radii, type scales, button styles, or one-off primitives unless nothing close exists
- Prefer shells already in use: `OnboardingLayout`, `AppBottomSheet`, inputs, `PrimaryButton` / `SecondaryButton`, `ScrollFadeView`
- Apply tokens, typography, icons, layering, and scroll-fade rules when composing UI
- In the change summary, flag what was guessed vs Figma-backed
